01:00:01.850 --> 01:00:04.890
Well, of course, Barbara wasn't executed in the final episode,

01:00:05.120 --> 01:00:07.680
and the Doctor and Vicky escaped by the skin of their teeth

01:00:07.680 --> 01:00:09.980
from being burned at the stake of sorcerers.

01:00:10.790 --> 01:00:14.420
The Crusade was written by Doctor Who's first script editor, David Whittaker,

01:00:14.820 --> 01:00:17.740
and is a good example of the purely historical stories

01:00:17.740 --> 01:00:21.520
which were entertaining, educational, and highly popular at the time.

01:00:22.650 --> 01:00:26.230
Now, it's easy to think that Doctor Who has reached international appeal more recently,

01:00:26.370 --> 01:00:29.970
but in fact, in the 1960s, foreign sales of Doctor Who were really...

01:00:30.000 --> 01:00:34.950
quite healthy. And here from the archive is an example of one of the episodes specially

01:00:34.950 --> 01:00:36.070
dubbed into Arabic.

01:01:00.124 --> 01:01:02.124
Al-Fatiha

01:01:02.204 --> 01:01:04.204
What are you talking about?

01:01:05.372 --> 01:01:11.692
You said that the power of the solar system works to expel the power from my ship.

01:01:14.268 --> 01:01:15.268
It's the truth

01:01:16.220 --> 01:01:18.220
Here we are at the beginning.

01:01:19.196 --> 01:01:21.796
for the appearance of a new solar system

01:01:23.868 --> 01:01:26.188
The atoms are moving towards each other

01:01:27.548 --> 01:01:29.348
